I'm going for the foodless atheist polyselfless survivor Tourist who 
will eventually survive on potions with a horn of plenty and the PYEC.

First, of course, I have to find a ring of slow digestion.  The game
won't last much more than a thousand turns without it; and after the
first few hundred turns, it's probably too late anyway.

So I ran some calculations which may interest others.
Tourist have the benefit of 4 scrolls of magic mapping, so I can explore 
four levels fairly quickly.
I generated the first four levels of 275000 games of Nethack.
There were 15832 rings of slow digestion, of which 10376 were in shops,
and 115 were in walled-in closets (sob).
There were 1894 wands of wishing, of which 898 were in shops, and 17 
were in walled-in closets (the poor bastards!).

With the scrolls I can find shops *very* quickly; in about 4% of games I 
should find the needed ring, or a wand of wishing, in one of the shops 
on levels 2, 3, and 4.  Another 2% will have it just lying around, but 
exploring all four levels tends to take too long.  I've settled on 
finding the shops, and then dipping fountains, and then exploring, as 
seeming like the most likely way to get a good start.

The very first Ciompi found a ring of slow digestion lying around on 
